        "A similar query on other tables: paid orders per customer, keeping customers with none. SELECT cu.customer_id, COUNT(DISTINCT o.order_id) AS paid_orders FROM customers AS cu LEFT JOIN orders AS o ON o.customer_id = cu.customer_id AND o.status = 'paid' GROUP BY cu.customer_id. The status filter sits in ON, so a customer without paid orders keeps one row with NULLs and gets 0. COALESCE(expression, 0) turns a NULL result into 0."
